---
import Shell from '../components/Martlet.astro';import {localPath as href} from '../paths';
const page={id:'journal',title:'Notes from the workshop.',eyebrow:'Journal',summary:'Reading, making, and keeping a design language coherent.'};
---
<Shell page={page} href={href} base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} renderContent={false}><div class="journal-list"><h2><a href={href('/examples/article/')}>What a shell should own</a></h2><p>A masthead holds context, navigation names destinations, and the reading column gives an argument room. Those relationships survive a different rendering engine.</p><p><a href={href('/examples/archive/')}>Explore the fictional field notes</a> for a complete publication collection.</p></div></Shell>
